Security audit (module: updater/server.ts):
  Threat model: a process on the host that managed to bind-mount the
  unix socket trying to issue /apply or /warm-pull.

  - All three endpoints (/apply, /warm-pull, /status) gated by
    verifyRequest(headers, rawBody) BEFORE any branch on path.
    A missing/expired/forged HMAC short-circuits with 401.
  - rawBody is read ONCE and passed to both the HMAC verifier and
    JSON.parse — no chance of "verify one buffer, execute another".
  - /aply concurrency: currentJob global serializes; second /apply
    while a job runs returns 409. No race window where two jobs
    write the same .env.version pin.
  - /warm-pull does NOT touch currentJob or .env.version — it only
    docker-pulls. Safe to call repeatedly under serialization.
  - Rollback path re-pins fromVersion + composes up; failure of
    rollback flips status to "failed" (not "rolled-back"), distinct
    from the success case, so the admin UI can render "human
    intervention needed" vs "version is now safely on old version".
  - Container image digest verified via `docker image inspect
    --format {index .RepoDigests 0}}` AFTER pull — a compromised
    GHCR that swapped a tag would fail this check, not silently
    serve a malicious image.
  - Socket re-created on boot (existsSync → unlinkSync) — stale
    sockets from crashed previous run don't block startup.

  No vulns found. Handshake gate is unconditional, rawBody binding
  is correct, concurrency contract holds.

